{"author":{"id":"2f242a7e7f2592f8909954a77fabece74f6e8cc197182647ed3b15ea8e3878af"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791027327,"nonce":"v04czgys9GU4MOPWSiczF310Fwc=","title":"the clipboard carries only plain text","message":"ashui asks (2026-10-03) to copy and paste typed data: images (PNG first), rich text (HTML first, RTF), and file lists, writing several representations at once so the receiving app takes the richest it understands. Plain text (7f00aa1f4bd3dafbabafde6922eb6f6762003289bb5139d0500182a338fea33f) stays the floor. Not blocking: ashui builds on plain text meanwhile.\n\nA shape that needs nothing new from x-idl:\n\n    /// The clipboard's types, as MIME types, best first.\n    fn clipboardTypeCount() -\u003e i32;          // count and index, as monitors\n    fn clipboardType(index: i32) -\u003e Text;\n    /// The bytes for one type, or none.\n    fn clipboardData(mimeType: Text) -\u003e OptionalBytes;   // enum { None, Some { bytes: Buffer } }\n    /// Several representations written at once.\n    trait ClipboardItems { fn new() -\u003e Box\u003cClipboardItems\u003e; fn add(this, mimeType: Text, bytes: Buffer); fn write(this) -\u003e bool; }\n\nFiles travel as text/uri-list. A list result and a list-of-pairs argument would read better in Haxe, but are not x-idl shapes today.\n\nwindow_clipboard (the text backend) has no typed data; arboard has text, images as RGBA and HTML, but reaches Wayland only through wlr-data-control, which GNOME lacks. Typed data on every desktop means each platform directly:\n\n- macOS: NSPasteboard through objc2-app-kit, UTIs mapped to MIME (public.png, public.html, public.rtf, public.file-url).\n- Windows: clipboard-win with registered formats (\"PNG\", \"HTML Format\" with its header, \"Rich Text Format\") and CF_HDROP for files.\n- X11: selection targets through x11rb, serving each MIME target, INCR for large payloads, a thread owning the selection.\n- Wayland: smithay-client-toolkit's data device on the app's own connection, an offer per MIME type, set with a recent input serial (as the text clipboard already needs).\n- Page: navigator.clipboard.write with a ClipboardItem per type, gated on activation; reading is asynchronous, as for text (855a063f7faba8453af86da5929f6044a2ff09d26f804bca29f9dadf78613a29).\n\nTesting: the desktop test writes text/plain plus text/html plus image/png and reads each back, under sway, X11, GNOME and Windows; on macOS against an AppKit reader.","files":null}]}